Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||04-09-2001||04:46 PM||||For my astronomy class (elective..) I have to do a project on a constellation. I was assigned Orion.. I had to take some time lapse photos of the constellation, and I just got them scanned into the computer. How's this for my first try at photographing stars? My dad's pretty good with photography so he helped me.<P>Anyone else ever taken pictures like this? Any tips/suggestions would be awesome.. I'd like to take some more this summer, and see if I can get some really good ones. My astronomy professor said he has a Pentax camera adapter for a telescope, so maybe I could even get some photos of a nebula or something..<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.digitalfusion.on.ca/constellation4.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
